---
import Since from '../../components/Since.astro';
import Snippet from '../../components/Snippet.astro';
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';

const html = `<!doctype html>
<meta charset="utf-8" />
<title>zvuk · stream</title>
<button id="play">Play</button>
<button id="pause">Pause</button>
<button id="fade">Fade out</button>
<input id="seek" type="range" min="0" max="1" step="0.001" value="0" />
<script type="module" src="./main.ts"></script>`;

const main = `import { createEngine, type StreamSound } from '@schmooky/zvuk';

const engine = createEngine({ buses: { ambience: { level: 0.6 } } });
const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id)!;
const seek = $('seek') as HTMLInputElement;

let rain: StreamSound | null = null;

$('play').onclick = async () => {
  await engine.unlock();
  // Not decoded: an <audio> element reads it progressively and its output is
  // routed into the ambience bus, so bus level, FX and ducking still apply.
  rain ??= engine.loadStream('rain', ['/audio/rain.webm', '/audio/rain.m4a'], { bus: 'ambience' });
  rain.setVolume(1);
  // v2: play() says whether the browser let it start.
  const started = await rain.play({ loop: true });
  if (!started) {
    $('play').textContent = 'Tap to play'; // autoplay refused: retry from this gesture
    return;
  }
  console.log('streaming', rain.url); // the ladder entry actually in use
  rain.ended.then(() => console.log('rain stopped'));
};

$('pause').onclick = () => rain?.pause();

$('fade').onclick = async () => {
  if (!rain) return;
  await rain.fade({ to: 0, duration: 2 });
  rain.stop();
};

seek.oninput = () => {
  if (rain && rain.duration) rain.seek(Number(seek.value) * rain.duration);
};

setInterval(() => {
  if (rain && rain.duration && !rain.paused) seek.value = String(rain.currentTime / rain.duration);
}, 250);`;
---
<Docs
  title="StreamSound"
  description="A long ambience or music track played through an audio element instead of being decoded into memory. Two files to copy."
  eyebrow="Example"
>
  <p>
    The rain bed on this site is 68 seconds long. Decoded, that is about
    26 MB of PCM sitting in memory for a sound that never needs sample
    accuracy, and on iOS the decode itself stalls the page.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>engine.loadStream</code> returns a <code>StreamSound</code> right
    away, without fetching. The first <code>play()</code> builds an
    <code>&lt;audio&gt;</code> element and a
    <code>MediaElementAudioSourceNode</code>, and routes it into the bus.
  </p>
  <p>
    Three things changed in v2 <Since v="2.0" />. <code>play()</code>
    resolves <code>true</code> when the element is playing and
    <code>false</code> when the browser refused (autoplay before a gesture,
    or no playable source); 1.x resolved nothing either way. The URL ladder
    is ordered by <code>pickSourceOrder</code> and the element falls through
    to the next URL on a media error, with <code>url</code> saying which one
    it is on. And <code>ended</code> resolves when playback ends, because the file
    ran out (never, while looping), <code>stop()</code> ran, or the stream
    was disposed.
  </p>

  <h2>index.html</h2>
  <Snippet code={html} lang="html" title="index.html" />

  <h2>main.ts</h2>
  <Snippet code={main} lang="ts" title="main.ts" />

  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A stream can't be pitched, offset into a sprite region, or limited per voice; it has one playhead. Use <code>loadSound</code> for anything short.</li>
    <li><code>resolveAsset</code> doesn't apply to streams, which always read from the URL.</li>
    <li>The element is created on first play and can't move to another bus afterwards. <code>dispose()</code> releases it, and so do <code>engine.unload(name)</code> and loading another stream under the same name.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Related</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/guides/loading/">Loading sounds</a> on when to stream and when to decode.</li>
    <li><a href="/examples/music/">Music</a> for looped tracks with an intro and an outro.</li>
    <li><a href="/examples/">All examples</a></li>
  </ul>
</Docs>
